WEBVTT


00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:55.006
Ryan, Jeanette's on the phone.


00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:57.347
I'm not home.


00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.774
She's crying, Ryan.


00:02:00.886 --> 00:02:02.513
When isn't she crying?


00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.988
W-- Well, can you just talk to her?


00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:09.495
Otherwise she's gonna keep me
on the phone half the night.


00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:11.395
Hang up on her, Wade.


00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:16.159
I can't... do that.
Will you just talk to her?


00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:21.371
Just-- tell her I'm in the bathroom
and I'll call her back later.


00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:23.275
Please.


00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:26.340
I'm in the bathroom, Wade.


00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:40.786
Yeah, Jeanette?


00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:45.031
Yeah. Um, he says he's gonna...
be in the bathroom.


00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:46.259
He'll call you back.


00:02:48.634 --> 00:02:50.970
You know,
I should probably go over to my mom's.


00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:53.139
I was supposed to be there,
like, two hours ago.


00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:56.233
Hm. I wouldn't worry about her.


00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:58.977
She made a pact with the devil,
remember?


00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:10.956
Good rest ye merry cheating wives,
nothing you dismay.


00:03:10.956 --> 00:03:19.159
But that won't be a problem
if you never would have strayed.


00:03:23.235 --> 00:03:24.395
What do you think?


00:03:26.038 --> 00:03:28.029
Maybe I'll cut a record, huh?


00:03:30.142 --> 00:03:31.439
Think it's got potential?


00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:34.379
What are you doing here, Keith?


00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:38.809
What am I doing here?


00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:43.611
It's, uh... it's a good question.


00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:51.452
I, uh... I don't know. Not anymore.


00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:02.039
Oh my god.


00:04:03.175 --> 00:04:04.335
Relax, sweetheart.


00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:06.906
I'm not here to hurt you.


00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.177
Just want you to see something.


00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:17.512
No!


00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:34.002
Well look who finally decided to show up.


00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.431
You have any idea what time it is?


00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:39.837
Couldn't help it.
Something terrible happened. Keith s--


00:04:40.679 --> 00:04:42.882
I know. Larry called.


00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:45.146
He heard it on the police scanner.


00:04:47.653 --> 00:04:48.954
He always said he would.


00:04:48.954 --> 00:04:50.923
I just didn't believe him.


00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.258
I never thought for
a second he would have--


00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:56.854
Don't. Don't. Don't cry.


00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:01.362
It's too late for tears now.


00:05:03.035 --> 00:05:06.664
What you did to Keith,
there's no escaping it.


00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:12.907
Did you get your medication?


00:05:13.045 --> 00:05:15.104
I forgot.


00:06:12.771 --> 00:06:14.273
Shelley.


00:06:14.273 --> 00:06:18.444
Bruce! Oh my god! Hey!
What are you doing here?


00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:19.445
Moved back.


00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:19.945
You moved back--


00:06:19.945 --> 00:06:21.113
Just got here a couple days ago.


00:06:21.113 --> 00:06:23.816
Well, I never think you would come back,
living in Vegas and all.


00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:26.018
Yeah, Vegas didn't treat me so good.


00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:26.652
Oh.


00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:28.554
I got to like gambling a little too much.


00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:30.356
Been working up near
Truckee last couple years.


00:06:30.356 --> 00:06:31.557
Yeah? Doing...


00:06:31.557 --> 00:06:33.926
Law enforcement. If you can believe that.


00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:34.627
Very nice.


00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:36.629
I just transferred to Meadville.


00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:37.263
Great.


00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:39.031
Shelley, your order's up.


00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:40.498
Hold on a second, Bruce.


00:06:42.968 --> 00:06:45.571
Right. Here.


00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:50.142
Avocado andnoodles.
You guys good? Yeah.


00:06:50.142 --> 00:06:52.745
And- and you? What's new with you?
How's your mom?


00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:55.881
Um... pretty much the same, actually.


00:06:55.881 --> 00:06:56.882
And, and Keith?


00:06:56.882 --> 00:07:01.820
Sorry. That's, uh, that's actually
a long story, Bruce.


00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:03.622
Oh. You look good.


00:07:03.622 --> 00:07:05.824
Aw, thanks. So do you.


00:07:05.824 --> 00:07:07.960
Um, I was hoping I'd run into you.


00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:10.729
I've been so busy since I got back
I haven't seen anybody from school,


00:07:10.729 --> 00:07:11.830
and-- Shelley?


00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:15.334
Bucktoothed moron by
the window wants his check.


00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.670
Oh. Bruce, you kind of...
you caught me at a really busy time.


00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:19.605
Is there any way we can do this...


00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:23.943
Maybe we can get together sometime,
and- and really catch up.


00:07:23.943 --> 00:07:27.179
I would really like that.
I want to hear all about Vegas.


00:07:27.179 --> 00:07:29.148
Yeah. There's a lot to tell.


00:07:29.148 --> 00:07:30.240
Later, Bruce!


00:08:04.516 --> 00:08:06.984
Where's that good looking deputy
we just hired?


00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:16.095
I'm gonna go home and-
and grab a little sleep.


00:08:16.095 --> 00:08:17.730
I got a long night ahead of me.


00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:20.699
Me too. They put me on a double.
Can you believe that?


00:08:32.978 --> 00:08:36.949
Hey, excuse me, can you tell me
how to get to Pine Grove Avenue?


00:08:36.949 --> 00:08:39.952
Uh, yeah, just, uh go down to the light,


00:08:39.952 --> 00:08:42.421
and, uh, make a right, and, uh,
go about two blocks.


00:08:42.421 --> 00:08:43.422
You should see it right there.


00:08:43.422 --> 00:08:45.324
You look like a whore.


00:08:45.324 --> 00:08:49.094
You know, the kind of woman that makes
a man leave his wife and child.


00:08:49.094 --> 00:08:51.654
Kind of woman that makes a man
take his own life.


00:08:52.431 --> 00:08:53.632
Who are you?


00:08:53.632 --> 00:08:57.369
You know it's- it's really not a problem
with me if you're a whore,


00:08:57.369 --> 00:09:01.169
but then again, I ain't one of
the ones you been hurtin'.


00:09:08.781 --> 00:09:10.049
You've never seen him before?


00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:11.073
Never.


00:09:12.518 --> 00:09:14.953
He- he doesn't sound like
anybody Jeanette would know.


00:09:14.953 --> 00:09:16.655
How do you know who Jeanette knows,
Ryan?


00:09:16.655 --> 00:09:19.691
He- he- he could be a hitman.
You know how crazy she is.


00:09:19.691 --> 00:09:20.859
She's not that crazy.


00:09:20.859 --> 00:09:23.829
Oh no? Calling us at three, four,
five o'clock in the morning, Ryan?


00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:26.265
Calling my own mother to
have her turn against me?


00:09:26.265 --> 00:09:27.733
Your mother was already against you.


00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:30.335
Yeah, well you know at least
she didn't get somebody to show up


00:09:30.335 --> 00:09:31.503
at my work and call me a whore.


00:09:31.503 --> 00:09:33.305
You don't know that was Jeanette.


00:09:33.305 --> 00:09:35.674
Who else would it be, Ryan?


00:09:35.674 --> 00:09:38.811
She's- she's- she's going around town
telling everybody lies about me.


00:09:38.811 --> 00:09:41.547
You know, people think I killed Keith.


00:09:41.547 --> 00:09:44.049
Nobody thinks you killed Keith.


00:09:44.049 --> 00:09:47.985
Everybody thinks that, Ryan,
or else they think you did it.


00:09:49.021 --> 00:09:52.524
I just- I'm going crazy.


00:09:52.524 --> 00:09:55.360
I'm going out of my mind, Ryan.


00:09:55.360 --> 00:10:01.492
Okay. Okay. Whoa. Come on.


00:10:04.002 --> 00:10:05.333
Why don't we just go out somewhere.


00:10:06.171 --> 00:10:09.308
I don't want to go out.
People just stare.


00:10:09.308 --> 00:10:12.111
Wade told me about this party way up
in Pulaski.


00:10:12.111 --> 00:10:12.811
Pulaski?


00:10:12.811 --> 00:10:15.473
Yes. Nobody knows us out there.


00:10:16.115 --> 00:10:18.083
We're supposed to get,
like, two feet of snow.


00:10:19.151 --> 00:10:20.948
I have four wheel drive.


00:10:32.631 --> 00:10:33.532
Larry, it's me.


00:10:33.532 --> 00:10:34.933
I know it's you.


00:10:34.933 --> 00:10:37.169
There's a thing called caller lD,
you know.


00:10:37.169 --> 00:10:39.238
Or are you too drunk to remember?


00:10:39.238 --> 00:10:40.506
Don't start with me.


00:10:40.506 --> 00:10:41.740
Hey, I didn't start anything.


00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:43.401
You called me.


00:10:44.009 --> 00:10:45.944
So what favor can I do for you?


00:10:45.944 --> 00:10:48.580
You really think I only call
if I want something, don't you?


00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:51.517
No, I don't think, I know.
So what is it?


00:10:51.517 --> 00:10:53.385
Are you listening to
your scanner right now?


00:10:53.385 --> 00:10:54.820
I'm always listening.


00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:58.857
Well, Shelley was supposed to come by
a couple hours ago, and she didn't.


00:10:58.857 --> 00:11:00.325
That's typical Shelley.


00:11:00.325 --> 00:11:02.995
Yeah, well,
she's a little later than usual,


00:11:02.995 --> 00:11:06.165
and I got a little worried, so...


00:11:06.165 --> 00:11:08.066
Well, I haven't heard anything
about any accidents.


00:11:08.066 --> 00:11:09.301
Does that set your mind at ease?


00:11:09.301 --> 00:11:10.435
It does.


00:11:10.435 --> 00:11:12.995
Good. Bitch.


00:11:15.374 --> 00:11:16.534
Jerk.


00:11:30.289 --> 00:11:33.859
Well, damn. Look at all that snow.


00:11:33.859 --> 00:11:36.054
You sure you don't want to
stay the night?


00:11:36.395 --> 00:11:38.931
No, we should get going before
it gets too bad.


00:11:38.931 --> 00:11:40.132
Already bad.


00:11:40.132 --> 00:11:42.566
We'll be fine.


00:11:47.005 --> 00:11:50.463
Go away! You're not welcome here.


00:11:52.277 --> 00:11:54.268
Hey, watch it!


00:12:01.086 --> 00:12:03.611
Friendly local morons.


00:12:31.984 --> 00:12:34.353
Damnit, open the door!


00:12:34.353 --> 00:12:36.855
I will break this damn door down.
Don't think I won't.


00:12:36.855 --> 00:12:38.257
Jeanette, he's not here.


00:12:38.257 --> 00:12:39.091
Yeah.


00:12:39.091 --> 00:12:41.059
Bull crap he's not.


00:12:44.062 --> 00:12:45.163
Where is he?


00:12:45.163 --> 00:12:47.633
I don't know.
I haven't seen him all night.


00:12:47.633 --> 00:12:52.271
I'm sick and damn tired of him
not picking up my phone calls.


00:12:52.271 --> 00:12:54.673
He is the father of my child.


00:12:54.673 --> 00:12:58.010
How does he know Eliot's
not sick or something?


00:12:58.010 --> 00:12:59.278
Is Eliot sick?


00:12:59.278 --> 00:13:00.812
That's not the damn point.


00:13:00.812 --> 00:13:04.283
The point is he's irresponsible...
running around with that slut,


00:13:04.283 --> 00:13:07.019
and ignoring his duty as a father.


00:13:07.019 --> 00:13:08.281
You want a beer?


00:13:20.899 --> 00:13:22.968
It's Jeanette, isn't it?


00:13:22.968 --> 00:13:23.802
Yeah.


00:13:23.802 --> 00:13:24.536
Oh my god!


00:13:24.536 --> 00:13:27.072
How many times is
she gonna call tonight?


00:13:27.072 --> 00:13:29.574
As many times as she calls
every other night.


00:13:29.574 --> 00:13:33.874
Why don't we just...
why don't we just keep going?


00:13:34.713 --> 00:13:37.616
Why don't we just run away, right now?


00:13:37.616 --> 00:13:38.450
Look, we can't do that, all right?


00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:40.952
I got a kid, and you have your mother
to take care of.


00:13:40.952 --> 00:13:42.020
Yeah, I don't care anymore.


00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:44.356
She can find somebody else
to look after her.


00:13:44.356 --> 00:13:45.757
You can call for Eliot later.


00:13:45.757 --> 00:13:48.385
Yeah.
Jeanette would never let that happen.


00:13:49.328 --> 00:13:51.096
Then let's steal him.


00:13:51.096 --> 00:13:54.862
Let's go over there right now
and take him.


00:13:55.534 --> 00:13:56.435
You want to?


00:13:56.435 --> 00:13:58.303
Yeah. What's to stop us?


00:13:58.303 --> 00:14:00.498
I mean, he's your son.


00:14:02.307 --> 00:14:04.509
How long has that car been behind us?


00:14:04.509 --> 00:14:05.477
What car?


00:14:05.477 --> 00:14:07.813
The one behind us.


00:14:07.813 --> 00:14:09.906
I never noticed.


00:14:10.482 --> 00:14:12.818
Just- just make the next turn you can.


00:14:12.818 --> 00:14:13.452
Why?


00:14:13.452 --> 00:14:15.943
Just do it.


00:14:20.592 --> 00:14:22.427
It's him.


00:14:22.427 --> 00:14:23.195
Who?


00:14:23.195 --> 00:14:24.229
The man outside the diner.


00:14:24.229 --> 00:14:27.756
It's him, Ryan. He's following us.


00:14:28.533 --> 00:14:29.368
You think?


00:14:29.368 --> 00:14:31.036
Yeah, I think.


00:14:31.036 --> 00:14:34.272
Oh my god,
he- he probably wants to kill us.


00:14:34.272 --> 00:14:37.309
He- he's gonna try to run us off
the road and kill us.


00:14:37.309 --> 00:14:38.009
Go faster.


00:14:38.009 --> 00:14:39.611
Ryan, you gotta go fast--
I can only go so fast in all this snow.


00:14:39.611 --> 00:14:41.545
Just- just- just -just--


00:14:46.885 --> 00:14:47.786
He must have run off the road.


00:14:47.786 --> 00:14:48.620
He disappeared.


00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:49.644
What--


00:14:50.155 --> 00:14:52.953
Oh my god, Ryan! Stop!
What--


00:14:53.325 --> 00:14:54.159
You hit him!


00:14:54.159 --> 00:14:55.026
I did not!


00:14:55.026 --> 00:14:57.429
Yes you did! Just stop the car.


00:14:57.429 --> 00:14:58.764
A minute ago you tell me to drive faster.
Now you want me--


00:14:58.764 --> 00:15:00.165
Just stop the truck, Ryan!


00:15:00.165 --> 00:15:01.359
Fine.


00:15:10.542 --> 00:15:12.407
Hello?


00:15:13.078 --> 00:15:14.880
Hello?


00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:16.939
Is anybody there?


00:15:17.983 --> 00:15:19.584
I'm sure I didn't hit anybody.


00:15:19.584 --> 00:15:22.075
Ryan, I saw him, okay?


00:15:23.889 --> 00:15:25.789
There's no blood.


00:15:28.894 --> 00:15:30.629
There, look! Look!


00:15:30.629 --> 00:15:31.196
Where?


00:15:31.196 --> 00:15:32.798
There.


00:15:32.798 --> 00:15:34.933
There's blood e- everywhere. Oh.


00:15:34.933 --> 00:15:36.067
Oh my god.


00:15:36.067 --> 00:15:36.902
Oh my god, you're right.


00:15:36.902 --> 00:15:39.004
Oh my- what- are you sure it was,
like, it was a person?


00:15:39.004 --> 00:15:40.405
It wasn't, like, a deer or something?


00:15:40.405 --> 00:15:43.341
I mean, I don't know, Ryan.
I just saw it for a second. It ju--


00:15:43.341 --> 00:15:45.332
Come here. Well, where is he?


00:15:45.844 --> 00:15:48.108
Hello?


00:15:50.182 --> 00:15:52.446
Where are you?


00:16:03.995 --> 00:16:07.692
Do you think we should call the sheriff?


00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.425
No.


00:16:12.938 --> 00:16:15.273
Because they'll think
we did it on purpose.


00:16:15.273 --> 00:16:16.675
Why- why would they think that?


00:16:16.675 --> 00:16:18.143
Because it was him.


00:16:18.143 --> 00:16:18.844
Who?


00:16:18.844 --> 00:16:20.779
That guy.
The guy from the diner earlier.


00:16:20.779 --> 00:16:21.379
It was him.


00:16:21.379 --> 00:16:23.515
I mean, I only saw it for a second,
but I'm pretty sure.


00:16:23.515 --> 00:16:26.918
Shelley, come on. How could it be him?


00:16:26.918 --> 00:16:30.655
How could he be behind us one second
and then in front of us the next?


00:16:30.655 --> 00:16:35.456
I don't know, okay?
But l- I really think it was him.


00:16:37.395 --> 00:16:39.865
You didn't happen to see the name of
the road we're on, did you


00:16:39.865 --> 00:16:42.767
Uh... why?


00:16:42.767 --> 00:16:45.670
I just got a little turned around,
that's all.


00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:47.672
You- you- do you need a map?


00:16:47.672 --> 00:16:51.768
No, Shelley, the map is not gonna do any
good if I don't know where I am.


00:16:54.446 --> 00:16:57.040
Well, are we lost?


00:16:57.916 --> 00:16:59.851
We're a little lost.


00:16:59.851 --> 00:17:02.843
Is that like being a little pregnant?


00:17:04.689 --> 00:17:07.425
No.
Look, we're gonna be okay, all right?


00:17:07.425 --> 00:17:10.161
We- we've been driving for, what,
an hour now?


00:17:10.161 --> 00:17:12.391
We can't be too far from home.


00:17:16.501 --> 00:17:18.901
Is that a car up there?


00:17:19.538 --> 00:17:21.640
Yeah.


00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:24.609
What's it doing in the middle of
the road with no lights on?


00:17:24.609 --> 00:17:27.679
May- maybe they're in trouble
and need some help.


00:17:27.679 --> 00:17:29.806
We could use a little help ourselves.


00:17:31.182 --> 00:17:32.843
Be right back.


00:18:02.113 --> 00:18:02.581
That's so weird.


00:18:02.581 --> 00:18:04.583
Weird? What was weird?


00:18:04.583 --> 00:18:07.085
Uh, there's insects inside the car.


00:18:07.085 --> 00:18:07.719
Insects?


00:18:07.719 --> 00:18:09.821
Yeah. Flies or something.


00:18:09.821 --> 00:18:11.156
No people? What--


00:18:11.156 --> 00:18:14.216
No. Nothing but flies.


00:18:16.695 --> 00:18:18.830
We're playing the songs of
the season here at KPOX,


00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:22.400
and we've got a big old storm
brewing outside right now.


00:18:22.400 --> 00:18:24.235
Hello?


00:18:24.235 --> 00:18:27.772
Miranda, it's Gayle. Shelley's mom?


00:18:27.772 --> 00:18:29.574
Oh. Hi.


00:18:29.574 --> 00:18:31.876
Has- has Shelley called
you by any chance?


00:18:31.876 --> 00:18:35.175
Uh, tonight? No, why?


00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:36.648
Well, I haven't heard from her,


00:18:36.648 --> 00:18:38.917
and I was, uh,
was getting a little concerned.


00:18:38.917 --> 00:18:42.287
It's snowing like
you can't believe outside.


00:18:42.287 --> 00:18:43.822
Oh, global warming.


00:18:43.822 --> 00:18:44.889
I'm sorry?


00:18:44.889 --> 00:18:47.826
We're gonna get a lot more snow because
of global warming.


00:18:47.826 --> 00:18:50.095
We're gonna get a lot more of everything.


00:18:50.095 --> 00:18:54.065
Sweetie, you might wanna renew
your subscription to Time Magazine,


00:18:54.065 --> 00:18:57.002
if you ever had one.


00:18:57.002 --> 00:19:01.371
Um... I also, I don't think that's
how global warming works.


00:19:02.207 --> 00:19:07.479
And if Shelley calls, I will make sure
that I don't get a hold of you.


00:19:07.479 --> 00:19:08.179
I'm sorry?


00:19:08.179 --> 00:19:11.916
Um, nothing.
I'm just gonna go to bed, okay?


00:19:11.916 --> 00:19:13.747
Have a good night.


00:19:18.590 --> 00:19:20.615
Painkiller.


00:19:21.192 --> 00:19:22.750
You bastard.


00:19:23.795 --> 00:19:27.565
The National Weather Service is calling
for as much as three feet of snow.


00:19:27.565 --> 00:19:28.266
And if we're lucky,


00:19:28.266 --> 00:19:32.037
they'll taper off before morning,
with temperatures as low as zero.


00:19:32.037 --> 00:19:34.164
Yeah, that's right, we're talking zero.


00:19:38.443 --> 00:19:39.878
Hey, hey, hey,
there's a sign right there.


00:19:39.878 --> 00:19:40.645
Where? Where?


00:19:40.645 --> 00:19:41.913
Right there, right there. Slow down.


00:19:41.913 --> 00:19:42.380
What?


00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:44.007
Roll down the wind--


00:19:44.883 --> 00:19:45.750
Yeah. You see it?


00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:48.412
No, I can't see anything.


00:19:48.787 --> 00:19:50.880
No, it's fine. I got it.


00:19:51.823 --> 00:19:52.585
All right.


00:20:27.959 --> 00:20:29.761
Ryan! Ryan!
What? Whoa, what happened?


00:20:29.761 --> 00:20:30.762
Just saw Keith.


00:20:30.762 --> 00:20:33.298
Hey, hey! It's okay.
What- what happened?


00:20:33.298 --> 00:20:36.096
Just go, Ryan!
Just start the car and let's go!


00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:51.149
Ryan! Ryan!


00:20:51.149 --> 00:20:51.816
What are you doing?


00:20:51.816 --> 00:20:52.417
Ryan!


00:20:52.417 --> 00:20:53.551
Get off of me!


00:20:53.551 --> 00:20:56.884
Ryan, Ryan, Ryan!
Kill us both! Stop it get off!


00:20:57.856 --> 00:20:58.948
Ah!


00:21:01.926 --> 00:21:02.984
Ow!


00:21:04.162 --> 00:21:06.431
I'm s- I'm sorry. I'm sorry.


00:21:06.431 --> 00:21:12.199
Ow! What- what-


00:21:18.009 --> 00:21:19.444
Wh- I'm sorry.


00:21:19.444 --> 00:21:23.148
There's somebody outside of the car,
and I know this sounds crazy,


00:21:23.148 --> 00:21:23.948
but I really think it's Keith.


00:21:23.948 --> 00:21:27.485
Stop it! We just need to get home.
Okay?


00:21:27.485 --> 00:21:33.685
We'll just get home,
and we'll be all- all better.


00:21:48.239 --> 00:21:49.365
Come on!


00:22:01.820 --> 00:22:03.755
Nine-one-one emergency.


00:22:03.755 --> 00:22:06.658
Hello? Hello? Hey, hey,
I'm- I'm stuck in the snow. Hello?


00:22:06.658 --> 00:22:07.792
You're stranded?


00:22:07.792 --> 00:22:09.160
Look, we really need some help out here.


00:22:09.160 --> 00:22:11.763
No, no, no, no, no. Who is that?


00:22:11.763 --> 00:22:13.198
I think he's coming back.


00:22:13.198 --> 00:22:14.632
Why do you think he's coming back?


00:22:14.632 --> 00:22:16.434
Baby, are you sure the doors are locked?


00:22:16.434 --> 00:22:17.435
Hold the doors.


00:22:17.435 --> 00:22:18.369
Yes, sweetheart, the doors are locked.


00:22:18.369 --> 00:22:21.506
Sir? Sir, who's in the car with you?


00:22:21.506 --> 00:22:23.474
Come on! Hel- who- are you there?


00:22:23.474 --> 00:22:25.577
Sir, who do you have in the car with you?


00:22:25.577 --> 00:22:26.711
Uh, that's my girlfriend.


00:22:26.711 --> 00:22:30.181
And, uh, what is she talking about
somebody coming back?


00:22:30.181 --> 00:22:33.985
Look, no- nobody-- Look, we just- we may
have seen a couple people out here,


00:22:33.985 --> 00:22:36.888
and we think that they may be
trying to hurt us.


00:22:36.888 --> 00:22:38.623
And why would they want to do that?


00:22:38.623 --> 00:22:42.727
Well, you know,
I think-- l- we- we think...


00:22:42.727 --> 00:22:46.397
that... there- there may have been
an accident a while back.


00:22:46.397 --> 00:22:48.199
And- and- and we think that
the other driver,


00:22:48.199 --> 00:22:49.467
that he might be trying to hurt us.


00:22:49.467 --> 00:22:52.036
Because you hurt him in the accident?


00:22:52.036 --> 00:22:55.106
Maybe. But l- l- I don't even know
if there was an accident.


00:22:55.106 --> 00:22:56.274
Have you been drinking?


00:22:56.274 --> 00:22:58.343
No, no. I haven't had a drop to drink
all night long,


00:22:58.343 --> 00:22:59.644
and neither has my girlfriend.


00:22:59.644 --> 00:23:01.913
Okay. And exactly where are you?


00:23:01.913 --> 00:23:02.814
We're- we're- uh,


00:23:02.814 --> 00:23:04.782
we're- we're- we're near,
uh, Deer Tail Road.


00:23:04.782 --> 00:23:05.950
My girlfriend said she saw a sign
that said that said Deer Tail Road.


00:23:05.950 --> 00:23:07.185
Deer Tail Road.


00:23:07.185 --> 00:23:08.286
I saw a sign that said Deer Tail Road.
I saw--


00:23:08.286 --> 00:23:09.921
And that's- that should be about
a mile and a half from


00:23:09.921 --> 00:23:11.354
I saw it back there. I don't-


00:23:19.631 --> 00:23:23.968
Ten-twelve, we got a stranded vehicle
in the vicinity of.


00:23:23.968 --> 00:23:28.439
Yeah, we got a white jeep,
license plate three H-E-L five eight one,


00:23:28.439 --> 00:23:31.738
registered to a Ryan Edward Dunbar.


00:23:32.477 --> 00:23:36.114
Oh, man, Ryan, l- I haven't seen Ryan
since high school.


00:23:36.114 --> 00:23:38.016
Well, he and his girlfriend are stuck
in a ditch out about


00:23:38.016 --> 00:23:41.247
a mile and a half from twenty-eight
seventy-six Montpelier.


00:23:44.022 --> 00:23:45.890
Two eight seven six Montpelier?


00:23:45.890 --> 00:23:46.591
That's right.


00:23:46.591 --> 00:23:48.422
Did he happen to mention
his girlfriend's name?


00:23:49.560 --> 00:23:50.762
Uh, he didn't, no.


00:23:50.762 --> 00:23:53.431
Uh, but he said he thought they might
have been involved in a hit and run.


00:23:53.431 --> 00:23:55.667
He thought they might have been?


00:23:55.667 --> 00:23:57.368
That's right. That's what he said.


00:23:57.368 --> 00:24:01.005
Um, he thought maybe the other driver
was trying to harm them in some way.


00:24:01.005 --> 00:24:01.439
I don't know.


00:24:01.439 --> 00:24:04.169
It didn't make a hell of a lot of sense,
if you ask me.


00:24:37.642 --> 00:24:38.977
Oh.


00:24:38.977 --> 00:24:40.342
What do you want?


00:24:44.415 --> 00:24:45.616
You're blitzed out of your head, huh?


00:24:45.616 --> 00:24:49.153
No, I just almost fell over trying to
open the damn door.


00:24:49.153 --> 00:24:52.323
Oh, maybe if you weren't drinking
you wouldn't almost be falling.


00:24:52.323 --> 00:24:55.126
I'm crippled, Larry. Remember?


00:24:55.126 --> 00:24:56.718
Yeah, in more ways than one.


00:24:57.395 --> 00:24:59.697
Did you come all the way over here
just to insult me?


00:24:59.697 --> 00:25:01.733
No, but as long as I'm here,
I figured I might as well.


00:25:01.733 --> 00:25:02.700
That's hilarious.


00:25:02.700 --> 00:25:05.303
You're- you're- you're just a real riot.


00:25:05.303 --> 00:25:06.838
Well, you used to think so.


00:25:06.838 --> 00:25:08.539
Well I came to my senses.


00:25:08.539 --> 00:25:11.167
So if you're here to insult me,
just leave.


00:25:16.180 --> 00:25:18.273
Shelley's stuck in a ditch.


00:25:19.350 --> 00:25:20.018
What?


00:25:20.018 --> 00:25:22.086
I heard it on my scanner.


00:25:22.086 --> 00:25:23.421
Well how do you know it's her?


00:25:23.421 --> 00:25:25.089
Boyfriend's name is Ryan, right?


00:25:25.089 --> 00:25:27.291
Oh, that jerk. Don't remind me.


00:25:27.291 --> 00:25:29.761
Yeah.
Well, uh, he called police dispatch,


00:25:29.761 --> 00:25:31.596
gave your address and everything.


00:25:31.596 --> 00:25:32.997
And, sounds like they've been
in an accident.


00:25:32.997 --> 00:25:34.432
Uh, with somebody else, I mean.


00:25:34.432 --> 00:25:35.466
Well, is she okay?


00:25:35.466 --> 00:25:36.567
I didn't hear anything about
any injuries.


00:25:36.567 --> 00:25:39.058
All I heard was that
they're stuck in a ditch.


00:25:39.637 --> 00:25:41.806
Well, go pull her out.


00:25:41.806 --> 00:25:44.609
N- you know, the sheriff's on it.


00:25:44.609 --> 00:25:46.144
I- l- l- I was on my way home.


00:25:46.144 --> 00:25:47.745
I just thought maybe you'd like to know.


00:25:47.745 --> 00:25:49.781
Well, Larry, why can't
you just go pull her out?


00:25:49.781 --> 00:25:53.451
Because. I've been working
since seven o'clock this morning.


00:25:53.451 --> 00:25:54.719
I'm exhausted.


00:25:54.719 --> 00:25:56.120
I'm gonna go home and
get a little bit of shut eye.


00:25:56.120 --> 00:25:57.955
Oh, on a night like this?
Bull.


00:25:57.955 --> 00:25:59.057
You're not gonna go to sleep.


00:25:59.057 --> 00:26:01.218
There's too much business out there.


00:26:02.693 --> 00:26:03.528
You know, sheriff's on it.


00:26:03.528 --> 00:26:04.829
I'm- I'm on my way home.


00:26:04.829 --> 00:26:06.564
I just thought you might want to know.


00:26:06.564 --> 00:26:09.700
You're gonna leave my daughter stuck in
a ditch to get back at me?


00:26:09.700 --> 00:26:11.936
Oh, since when do you care
about your daughter?


00:26:11.936 --> 00:26:14.338
Since when do you care about anybody?


00:26:14.338 --> 00:26:16.636
I care about a lot of people.


00:26:17.809 --> 00:26:20.710
Fact, there's just one person
I don't care about.


00:26:26.484 --> 00:26:27.815
Always a pleasure, Gayle.


00:26:46.037 --> 00:26:47.629
Some tow truck driver.


00:26:57.181 --> 00:27:04.747
Dear God, please keep Shelley safe.
Please.


00:27:32.817 --> 00:27:34.341
Not without protection.


00:27:41.759 --> 00:27:44.626
I don't want to get pregnant,
stuck in this town forever.


00:28:06.317 --> 00:28:07.852
Are you sure you got
the location correct?


00:28:07.852 --> 00:28:09.520
Because I've been up and down Montpelier
two times already.


00:28:09.520 --> 00:28:11.756
I'm not seeing any stranded white jeep.


00:28:11.756 --> 00:28:13.124
You wanna get some more guys on this?


00:28:13.124 --> 00:28:14.853
Yeah, I think we better, yeah.


00:28:26.837 --> 00:28:28.236
Wanna hit this?


00:28:29.640 --> 00:28:31.369
Don't mind if I do.
Yeah.


00:28:34.078 --> 00:28:35.739
It's kind of weird that
he hasn't come home yet.


00:28:36.681 --> 00:28:38.046
I hope he's dead.


00:28:38.716 --> 00:28:39.808
Oh, you don't hope that


00:28:40.718 --> 00:28:41.912
No, I don't.


00:28:44.522 --> 00:28:49.289
But you know what,
I don't really love him anymore.


00:28:51.762 --> 00:28:54.424
If you woulda asked me that a month ago,
I would have said yeah.


00:28:55.666 --> 00:28:56.963
But not now.


00:28:58.636 --> 00:29:00.399
I started seeing someone else.


00:29:01.539 --> 00:29:02.733
Who?


00:29:03.341 --> 00:29:06.777
This guy. He really loves me, too.


00:29:07.578 --> 00:29:08.840
You want to see a picture of him?


00:29:18.256 --> 00:29:20.087
He is ugly.


00:29:21.359 --> 00:29:22.883
He is, isn't he?


00:29:26.931 --> 00:29:28.733
Nine-one-one emergency.


00:29:28.733 --> 00:29:30.034
Hey, yeah.


00:29:30.034 --> 00:29:35.006
This is, uh, this is Ryan Dunbar,
the guy who's stranded?


00:29:35.006 --> 00:29:35.973
I know who you are.


00:29:35.973 --> 00:29:38.609
We've got people out there
looking everywhere for you.


00:29:38.609 --> 00:29:40.338
Well, what's the hold up?


00:29:40.911 --> 00:29:41.946
We can't find you.


00:29:41.946 --> 00:29:43.814
Are you sure you gave us
the correct location?


00:29:43.814 --> 00:29:45.182
What's she saying?


00:29:45.182 --> 00:29:46.083
Uh, yeah- yeah.


00:29:46.083 --> 00:29:48.252
Wait, what's she saying?
Pretty sure.


00:29:48.252 --> 00:29:50.988
They said they can't find us.


00:29:50.988 --> 00:29:52.223
Well then, let's just walk.


00:29:52.223 --> 00:29:53.524
It's not that far.


00:29:53.524 --> 00:29:59.697
Wait, Ryan, did I hear her say
something about walking?


00:29:59.697 --> 00:30:01.756
Yeah. Yeah.


00:30:02.867 --> 00:30:04.268
Well, that's a very bad idea.


00:30:04.268 --> 00:30:06.837
It's five below right now.


00:30:06.837 --> 00:30:08.172
Doesn't feel that cold.


00:30:08.172 --> 00:30:08.873
Well, it is.


00:30:08.873 --> 00:30:11.309
And I'm not even adding
in the wind chill.


00:30:11.309 --> 00:30:13.504
You- you got your heater running, right?


00:30:14.011 --> 00:30:16.138
Yeah- yes. It's on.


00:30:16.714 --> 00:30:18.649
And you got plenty of gas?


00:30:18.649 --> 00:30:19.583
Full tank.


00:30:19.583 --> 00:30:20.718
Then just sit tight.


00:30:20.718 --> 00:30:22.153
We're gonna find you, you know.


00:30:22.153 --> 00:30:23.177
Don't worry about it.


00:30:27.058 --> 00:30:33.793
I wish l- I wish I could fall asleep,
and wake up in my own bed.


00:30:35.800 --> 00:30:38.202
You can fall asleep on my shoulder
if you want.


00:30:38.202 --> 00:30:40.102
No, it's not gonna happen.


00:30:41.272 --> 00:30:42.705
I can't sleep right now.


00:30:55.119 --> 00:31:00.458
My god. Bruce, how long has it been?


00:31:00.458 --> 00:31:01.792
A long time.


00:31:01.792 --> 00:31:03.627
You're working for the sheriff,
what do you know about that.


00:31:03.627 --> 00:31:06.528
Yeah, well, it's been interesting.


00:31:07.331 --> 00:31:08.532
Do you mind if I come in?


00:31:08.532 --> 00:31:09.965
Oh, of course.


00:31:10.434 --> 00:31:13.371
Uh, you're catching me
at kind of a weird--


00:31:13.371 --> 00:31:14.572
Yeah, I know.


00:31:14.572 --> 00:31:18.442
I've been out looking for her,
saw your lights on,


00:31:18.442 --> 00:31:20.745
thought I'd come by and see
if you knew where she might be.


00:31:20.745 --> 00:31:23.805
Me? Oh, she doesn't call me.


00:31:24.882 --> 00:31:28.953
You know, she stops by once a day
to bring me groceries,


00:31:28.953 --> 00:31:34.118
or help around the house,
but she doesn't call unless she has to.


00:31:34.525 --> 00:31:36.322
She doesn't really take my calls, either.


00:31:37.661 --> 00:31:42.733
You know,
I honestly think you were pretty lucky,


00:31:42.733 --> 00:31:44.496
not ending up marrying her.


00:31:45.236 --> 00:31:46.601
Well, I don't know about that.


00:31:47.104 --> 00:31:51.063
I do. You know about Keith, don't you?


00:31:52.276 --> 00:31:56.076
Blew his brains out. About a month ago.


00:31:58.482 --> 00:32:01.352
She'd already dumped him for that
criminal she's running around with.


00:32:01.352 --> 00:32:02.553
Uh, you mean Ryan?


00:32:02.553 --> 00:32:04.088
You know about him?


00:32:04.088 --> 00:32:08.959
Yeah. My mom filled me in.
I thought Ryan got married?


00:32:08.959 --> 00:32:14.098
He did. He did.
He left his wife and baby last summer,


00:32:14.098 --> 00:32:19.136
moved in with some drug addict friend of
his who lives out near the flats.


00:32:19.136 --> 00:32:21.105
They've both had run ins with the law.


00:32:21.105 --> 00:32:28.170
I had Lynn pull Ryan's record,
and... DUl, bar fight, nothing major.


00:32:29.280 --> 00:32:31.749
I didn't raise Shelley to run around
with somebody like that.


00:32:31.749 --> 00:32:35.052
But oh, no, she loves him to death.


00:32:35.052 --> 00:32:39.390
She didn't even come to her senses after
Keith killed himself.


00:32:39.390 --> 00:32:41.620
Oh, she was always selfish like that.


00:32:42.393 --> 00:32:44.224
She wasn't selfish, Gayle.


00:32:44.762 --> 00:32:49.199
Like hell. You remember what happened
the night of my accident?


00:32:50.100 --> 00:32:56.474
I mean, I'm almost dead in a car wreck,
my spine and my legs are crushed,


00:32:56.474 --> 00:32:58.309
and they- they ask me
who should they call,


00:32:58.309 --> 00:32:59.510
and I said of course call my daughter.


00:32:59.510 --> 00:33:02.980
And they call her,
and she didn't show up at the hospital


00:33:02.980 --> 00:33:04.348
until nine or ten the next morning.


00:33:04.348 --> 00:33:07.718
I mean, my god,
her own mother, almost dead,


00:33:07.718 --> 00:33:11.322
and she can't even be bothered to
show up at the hospital?


00:33:11.322 --> 00:33:12.584
That's not true.


00:33:13.524 --> 00:33:15.726
I was with Shelley that night.


00:33:15.726 --> 00:33:17.523
And I drove her to the hospital.


00:33:18.262 --> 00:33:20.865
They wouldn't let her in to see you.


00:33:20.865 --> 00:33:23.167
We both stayed up all night waiting for
you to get out of surgery.


00:33:23.167 --> 00:33:26.270
It had been me,
and Shelley had been in an accident,


00:33:26.270 --> 00:33:29.262
they would have had to hold me down
to keep me from seeing her.


00:33:31.442 --> 00:33:34.002
She wasn't even that upset
when I did see her.


00:33:34.578 --> 00:33:36.944
Come on, mom. Gotta eat something.


00:33:37.681 --> 00:33:39.046
We're gonna go to therapy.


00:33:41.118 --> 00:33:42.786
Oh, what's the point?


00:33:42.786 --> 00:33:45.084
It's not like I'm ever gonna walk again.


00:33:45.556 --> 00:33:46.390
That's not true.


00:33:46.390 --> 00:33:48.759
You just- you gotta
have the right attitude.


00:33:48.759 --> 00:33:50.694
Hon, I'm still gonna be handicapped.


00:33:50.694 --> 00:33:53.857
I mean, how am I supposed to
take care of myself?


00:33:55.299 --> 00:33:58.462
I wish your grandmother was still alive.


00:33:58.602 --> 00:34:01.405
And Larry, he's no good.


00:34:01.405 --> 00:34:05.075
That's not true. Larry loves you.


00:34:05.075 --> 00:34:06.508
You should marry Larry.


00:34:08.379 --> 00:34:14.952
He's not gonna marry me.
Not now. And you.


00:34:14.952 --> 00:34:18.022
You're gonna run off to college in
a few months and forget all about me.


00:34:18.022 --> 00:34:20.786
I'm not gonna run off to college, mom.


00:34:21.859 --> 00:34:24.161
If you need me, I'm gonna be here.


00:34:24.161 --> 00:34:27.289
Just- don't guilt me into it.


00:34:27.965 --> 00:34:33.096
Guilt? Sweetie, I'm not trying to guilt
you into anything.


00:34:34.538 --> 00:34:35.732
Well, you know Shelley.


00:34:37.041 --> 00:34:38.531
She had a lot of plans.


00:34:39.877 --> 00:34:42.311
I guess that's part of the reason
why she broke up with me.


00:34:43.681 --> 00:34:45.114
I wasn't ambitious enough.


00:34:45.883 --> 00:34:49.444
That's funny, you're the one
that ended up leaving.


00:34:50.054 --> 00:34:51.214
Well, I'm back now.


00:34:52.423 --> 00:34:55.051
And to tell you the truth,
she's a big part of the reason why.


00:34:56.126 --> 00:34:58.596
I guess I was kind of hoping
that one way or another


00:34:58.596 --> 00:35:01.963
we'd find our way back to each other.


00:35:04.201 --> 00:35:05.634
You know, I think you could.


00:35:07.371 --> 00:35:08.539
You're a deputy now.


00:35:08.539 --> 00:35:13.344
I mean, you, uh,
figure out how to put away this Ryan


00:35:13.344 --> 00:35:17.178
and I think there could be a little hope.


00:35:35.299 --> 00:35:36.200
Horizon Unlimited,


00:35:36.200 --> 00:35:39.103
can I have the name and phone number
you're calling from please?


00:35:39.103 --> 00:35:42.506
This is the Delmore County Sheriff's
dept in Meadville, California.


00:35:42.506 --> 00:35:45.643
